            "result_text": "The regex pattern has been saved. Here's how it works:\n\n**IPv4 Validation** (octet pattern: `25[0-5]|2[0-4][0-9]|1[0-9]{2}|[1-9]?[0-9]`):\n- `25[0-5]`: 250-255\n- `2[0-4][0-9]`: 200-249\n- `1[0-9]{2}`: 100-199\n- `[1-9]?[0-9]`: 0-99 (no leading zeros)\n\n**Date Validation** (per month):\n- **31-day months** (01,03,05,07,08,10,12): days 01-31\n- **30-day months** (04,06,09,11): days 01-30\n- **February** (02): days 01-29\n\n**Pattern Logic**:\n1. `(?=.*IPv4)` - Positive lookahead ensures an IPv4 address exists on the line\n2. `.*?` - Non-greedy match to find the first candidate date\n3. `(date)` - Capture the date (only content within parentheses is returned by `re.findall`)\n4. `(?!.*date)` - Negative lookahead ensures no other date follows on the same line\n\nWord boundaries (`\\b`) prevent matches like \"1134-12-1234\" (where no valid IPv4 exists) or \"error-2024-01-15\" when preceded by alphanumerics."
        }
